From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: 8192xb: raise the ADC RCK offset for timing code 0x1b

Dies with ADC timing code 0x1b used RCK offset 0xc and reset count 0x9
at 20/40 MHz, as in the older vendor tables. The vendor firmware on the
HG325AX30 programs 0xf and 0xa on the same die. On that board at HE40
the higher values raised RX throughput by about 18% (142 to 167 Mbit/s
over five rounds) with TX unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/rtw8192xb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/rtw8192xb.c
@@ -654,7 +654,8 @@ static const struct rtw8192xb_adc_cfg rtw8192xb_adc_cfgs[] = {
 	{0x19, 2, 0x4, 0xf, 8, 2, 0xa, 3},
 	{0x11, 2, 0x5, 0xf, 8, 2, 0xa, 3},
 	{0x09, 2, 0x3, 0xf, 8, 2, 0xa, 3},
-	{0x1b, 3, 0xc, 0xc, 8, 2, 0x9, 0},
+	/* 0x1b: RCK offset and reset count as in newer vendor firmware */
+	{0x1b, 3, 0xc, 0xf, 8, 2, 0xa, 0},
 	{0x1a, 3, 0xe, 0xf, 5, 0, 0x9, 0},
 	{0x12, 3, 0xd, 0xf, 5, 0, 0x9, 0},
 	{0x0a, 3, 0xc, 0xf, 5, 0, 0x9, 0},
